{"blocks":[["Arturia/MCC/UG/03%20Working%20with%20Templates/03%20Project%20and%20Template%20Browser/02%20Build%20Library/","source-block-373","Use Recall From to copy changed device memory into a new User Template. MCC gives it a timestamped name, which can be renamed.",["3.3.2. Building a library"]],["Arturia/MCC/UG/03%20Working%20with%20Templates/03%20Project%20and%20Template%20Browser/02%20Build%20Library/","source-block-503","The User Templates area can hold a library of presets, patterns, or sequences beyond the device’s capacity.",["3.3.2. Building a library"]],["Arturia/MCC/UG/03%20Working%20with%20Templates/03%20Project%20and%20Template%20Browser/03%20Working%20Memory/","source-block-341","3.3.3. The Working Memory / Working Project",[]],["Arturia/MCC/UG/03%20Working%20with%20Templates/03%20Project%20and%20Template%20Browser/03%20Working%20Memory/","source-block-389","When synced, Working Memory represents the device’s active memory and most MCC edits also reach the device.",["3.3.3. The Working Memory / Working Project"]],["Arturia/MCC/UG/03%20Working%20with%20Templates/03%20Project%20and%20Template%20Browser/03%20Working%20Memory/","source-block-502","When unsynced, Working Memory is a staging area. MCC edits do not automatically change the device.",["3.3.3. The Working Memory / Working Project"]],["Arturia/MCC/UG/03%20Working%20with%20Templates/03%20Project%20and%20Template%20Browser/03%20Working%20Memory/","source-block-604","Arturia/MCC/UG/03 Working with Templates/03 Project and Template Browser/03 Working Memory/01 Live Editing",["3.3.3. The Working Memory / Working Project"]],["Arturia/MCC/UG/03%20Working%20with%20Templates/03%20Project%20and%20Template%20Browser/03%20Working%20Memory/","source-block-718","Arturia/MCC/UG/03 Working with Templates/03 Project and Template Browser/03 Working Memory/02 Drag and Drop",["3.3.3. The Working Memory / Working Project"]],["Arturia/MCC/UG/03%20Working%20with%20Templates/03%20Project%20and%20Template%20Browser/03%20Working%20Memory/01%20Live%20Editing/","source-block-274","3.3.3.1. Live editing",[]],["Arturia/MCC/UG/03%20Working%20with%20Templates/03%20Project%20and%20Template%20Browser/03%20Working%20Memory/01%20Live%20Editing/","source-block-300","On a Sync capable device, MCC edits to the loaded memory are sent to the hardware.",["3.3.3.1. Live editing"]],["Arturia/MCC/UG/03%20Working%20with%20Templates/03%20Project%20and%20Template%20Browser/03%20Working%20Memory/01%20Live%20Editing/","source-block-573","An asterisk beside a Template name means the computer copy has unsaved edits. Use Save or Save As.",["3.3.3.1. Live editing"]],["Arturia/MCC/UG/03%20Working%20with%20Templates/03%20Project%20and%20Template%20Browser/03%20Working%20Memory/02%20Drag%20and%20Drop/","source-block-273","3.3.3.2. Drag and drop",[]],["Arturia/MCC/UG/03%20Working%20with%20Templates/03%20Project%20and%20Template%20Browser/03%20Working%20Memory/02%20Drag%20and%20Drop/","source-block-300","Drag an item or an entire Template from the browser to Working Memory to transmit it to the device. Some products also accept subcomponents such as a Controller Map.",["3.3.3.2. Drag and drop"]],["Arturia/MCC/UG/03%20Working%20with%20Templates/03%20Project%20and%20Template%20Browser/04%20Revise%20Template/","source-block-239","3.3.4. Revise a Template",[]],["Arturia/MCC/UG/03%20Working%20with%20Templates/03%20Project%20and%20Template%20Browser/04%20Revise%20Template/","source-block-268","Select an archived Template to edit it in MCC. Save or Save As preserves changed computer data.",["3.3.4. Revise a Template"]],["Arturia/MCC/UG/03%20Working%20with%20Templates/03%20Project%20and%20Template%20Browser/04%20Revise%20Template/01%20While%20Synced/","source-block-273","3.3.4.1. While synced",[]],["Arturia/MCC/UG/03%20Working%20with%20Templates/03%20Project%20and%20Template%20Browser/04%20Revise%20Template/01%20While%20Synced/","source-block-299","Selecting a Template sends its data to the connected device. Further MCC edits also affect the hardware; an asterisk signals unsaved Template changes.",["3.3.4.1. While synced"]],["Arturia/MCC/UG/03%20Working%20with%20Templates/03%20Project%20and%20Template%20Browser/04%20Revise%20Template/02%20Not%20Synced/","source-block-275","3.3.4.2. Not synced",[]],["Arturia/MCC/UG/03%20Working%20with%20Templates/03%20Project%20and%20Template%20Browser/04%20Revise%20Template/02%20Not%20Synced/","source-block-299","Edit an archived Template in MCC, then save it. To hear the result on the hardware, drag the revised Template to Working Memory or use Store To.",["3.3.4.2. Not synced"]],["Arturia/MCC/UG/03%20Working%20with%20Templates/04%20Store%20To%20and%20Recall%20From/","source-block-189","3.4. Store To / Recall From",[]],["Arturia/MCC/UG/03%20Working%20with%20Templates/04%20Store%20To%20and%20Recall%20From/01%20Store%20To/","source-block-228","3.4.1. The Store To button",[]],["Arturia/MCC/UG/03%20Working%20with%20Templates/04%20Store%20To%20and%20Recall%20From/01%20Store%20To/","source-block-259","Select a local Template, then press Store To to transmit all of its data to the device when Sync is off or unsupported.",["3.4.1. The Store To button"]],["Arturia/MCC/UG/03%20Working%20with%20Templates/04%20Store%20To%20and%20Recall%20From/01%20Store%20To/","source-block-382","When synced, selecting the Template itself transmits it.",["3.4.1. The Store To button"]],["Arturia/MCC/UG/03%20Working%20with%20Templates/04%20Store%20To%20and%20Recall%20From/02%20Recall%20From/","source-block-327","3.4.2. Recall edited data from the device",[]],["Arturia/MCC/UG/03%20Working%20with%20Templates/04%20Store%20To%20and%20Recall%20From/02%20Recall%20From/","source-block-373","Recall From copies the device data into a new timestamped local Template. Rename the copy if a descriptive name is useful.",["3.4.2. Recall edited data from the device"]],["Arturia/MCC/UG/03%20Working%20with%20Templates/04%20Store%20To%20and%20Recall%20From/03%20Template%20Utilities/","source-block-228","3.4.3. Template utilities",[]]],"format_version":5}